# The Journey Feature — Implementation Plan

## Overview
Build an immersive, story-driven Git learning path with 30 progressive chapters. The user follows a continuous project narrative, unlocking skills and earning XP as they complete chapters.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Data Layer
#### [NEW] `data/journey.ts`
- 30 chapters grouped into 6 acts (5 chapters each)
- Each chapter: `id`, `title`, `act`, `description`, `narrative`, `lesson` (markdown content), `commands[]`, `skill`, `xpReward`, `difficulty`
- Acts: Genesis → Branching → Collaboration → Time Travel → Advanced → Mastery
- Type exports: `Chapter`, `Act`, `journeyChapters`, `journeyActs`

---

### 2. Components
#### [NEW] `components/journey/journey-map.tsx`
- Visual vertical timeline/path showing all 30 chapters
- Chapters grouped by Act with act headers
- Completed/current/locked states with animations
- Click to navigate to chapter

#### [NEW] `components/journey/chapter-card.tsx`
- Card component for individual chapters in the map
- Shows title, difficulty badge, XP reward, skill icon
- Animated completion state (checkmark, glow)

#### [NEW] `components/journey/journey-progress-bar.tsx`
- Overall journey progress indicator
- Shows current act, chapters completed, total XP

#### [NEW] `components/journey/skill-tree.tsx`
- Visual display of unlocked skills
- Grid of skill icons with locked/unlocked states

#### [NEW] `components/journey/chapter-content.tsx`
- Renders chapter lesson content (markdown)
- "Complete Chapter" button at bottom
- Navigation between chapters

